why Every Alliance quest of Dire Maul's three wings in one run, lead-ins included.

# Dire Maul's Alliance quests in one guide: Pix Xizzix in Booty Bay (from
# level 60), the goods for Knot's suit, Rabine Saturna in Moonglade and the
# Reliquary of Purity in Silithus, Feathermoon and Azj'Tordin in Feralas, the
# three wings one after the other (with short returns into a wing where a
# quest asks for it), then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over,
# so the guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chains:
# - Latronicus Moonspear's 7488 Lethtendris's Web; Scholar Runethorn's 7482
#   Elven Legends; Azj'Tordin's 7441 Pusillin and the Elder Azj'Tordin.
# - Rabine Saturna's 5527 A Reliquary of Purity -> 5526 Shards of the
#   Felvine.
# - Inside: the Shen'dralar Ancient's 7461 The Madness Within -> 7462 The
#   Treasure of the Shen'dralar; Knot Thimblejack's 5525 Free Knot! and 5518
#   The Gordok Ogre Suit; Stomper Kreeg's 5528 The Gordok Taste Test; Captain
#   Kromcrush's 7703 Unfinished Gordok Business; for Mages of level 60,
#   Lorekeeper Lydros' 7463 Arcane Refreshment; the class books (7498 to
#   7506), which bosses drop and the lorekeepers take.
# - Pix Xizzix's 96076 In Demand - Ancient Elven Curiosities (level 60).
#
# Left out: 7494 Feathermoon Stronghold (a breadcrumb from the capitals, off
# this guide's way); 97009 and 97010 Blind Vengeance (Mount Hyjal quests with
# nothing in Dire Maul); 1318 Unfinished Gordok Business (no giver in the
# data; Kromcrush's 7703 is in); the repeatable 1193, 5519, 7429 and the
# Librams 7483 to 7485; 7507 Foror's Compendium and Quel'Serrar (it needs
# Onyxia); 7581 The Prison's Bindings, 7631 Dreadsteed of Xoroth, 7643 and
# 7647 (the warlock and paladin epic mount chains); 8948, 8949, 8950, 8967
# and 8990 (the Dungeon Set 2 and Valthalak chains); the off-page profession,
# Midsummer and Thorium Brotherhood quests.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, the NPCs or the objects
# inside, so their goals stand at the gate (@59.2,45.1, Feralas) with
# `group 5`. The client's group finder lists three wings, each its own
# instance with its own door in the ruins: East (levels 54 to 60, the
# Warpwood Quarter), West (56 to 60, the Athenaeum) and North (56 to 60, the
# Gordok wing); the guide takes them in that order, the bosses in the
# client's dungeon journal's order within them. Every quest goal is counted
# by the quest log, so a group that takes them in another order still gets
# each step ticked. Most of these quests ask for level 56, so the guide does.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The wings' names come from the quest texts.
#   The Felvine Shard comes from the Felvine, the Gauntlet of Gordok Might
#   from The Prince's Chest, the Ogre Tannin from a basket; the data has no
#   source for the Sealed Reliquary itself.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json): the Dire Maul gate.
# - The wings and their levels: the client's group finder; the bosses: its
#   dungeon journal (as Polestar's Codex page holds it).
# INGAME: where in the wings do Knot, Kreeg, Kromcrush, the Shen'dralar
#   Ancient, the lorekeepers, the Felvine and The Prince's Chest stand?

